## User preferences

- When requesting 「内部のバグや、危険性」 and release-ready laptop/iPad/smartphone UI -> report code safety, real-screen/device QA, and release blockers separately; do not collapse browser-width checks into physical-device validation. [Task 1]
- When the user asks 「こちら書き出しておいてくれますか」 -> preserve major review conclusions, validation, and remaining blockers in a handoff Markdown. [Task 1]
- For performance audio, use terminal-local files; do not send tracks to external streaming or shared sessions by default. [Task 1]
- For independent release audits, preserve dirty worktrees and keep writes isolated to a new run report directory; do not modify app files, JSON, settings, history, generated artifacts, public targets, secrets, or deployment state. [Task 2]

## Reusable knowledge

- `shosai-app` is the Git root; `index.html` is authoritative and `stage.html` is generated. After HTML changes run `python3 build_stage.py`, then `python3 build_stage.py --check`; never directly edit `stage.html`. [Task 1]
- Audio blobs live in IndexedDB `shosai-stage-audio` / `tracks`; project JSON stores metadata, track ID, and scene `audioTrackId` only. A missing track on another device must say it is absent locally and require reconnect; preserve position across adjacent same-track scenes, and verify metadata before reconnecting. [Task 1]
- Task 1 established a local candidate with 415 Node tests, 34 MCP tests, build check, JS syntax check, and `git diff --check`, but left P0 questions around worker auth, `?fresh`, pre-join backup failure, and Mac AI-edit revision conflict. [Task 1]
- Task 2 re-audited those blockers in `show-creative-ideas/shosai-app/overnight-runs/2026-08-22-stage-sketch-release-reaudit/`: worker auth now fails closed with 503 for production-secret misconfiguration, `?fresh` is localhost/file-only with confirmation, session entry aborts before guest-role change if shelving fails, and the Mac bridge has revision-conflict/project-lock/archive/trusted-origin/external-navigation guards. Verification passed with 447 Node tests, 34 MCP tests, JS syntax checks, `python3 build_stage.py --check`, `git diff --check`, and no new object-placement findings; release still stayed blocked because the temporary-copy native self-test exited 134, the tracked-diff fingerprint changed without attribution, and physical-device/public Worker/browser-equivalent/deployment checks were not done. [Task 2]
- When building a copied Mac app tree for non-destructive verification, exclude stale `mac-app/build`; including it can break compilation through stale Swift module-cache paths. [Task 2]
- Handoff: `docs/STAGE_SKETCH_RELEASE_REVIEW_2026-08-22.md` concludes 「ローカル候補版／リリース保留」; commit, push, and deploy were not performed. [Task 1]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Parent-workspace Git yields `fatal: not a git repository` -> run Git status/diff inside `shosai-app`, preserving its existing dirty worktree. [Task 1]
- A same-named but different reconnected audio file can silently bind incorrectly -> use `probeAudioFile` / `identityDifference` and require confirmation when name differs or duration differs by more than 5% or 2 seconds. [Task 1]
- Mobile landscape canvas clipped after adding the audio strip -> use the `100dvh - 46px` height calculation and update the regression test; untracked `stage-audio-store.js` / tests must be deliberately included before any commit or distribution. [Task 1]
- Root `npm test` fails with `ENOENT` because `show-creative-ideas/shosai-app` has no root `package.json` -> use `cd mcp-server && npm test` for the MCP suite. [Task 2]
- If the tracked-diff fingerprint changes during a read-only audit and attribution is unclear, stop further verification and preserve the blocked decision rather than normalizing unexpected drift. [Task 2]

